let _markdown$d = "\n\n<CodeBlockTabs defaultValue=\"Install\">\n  <CodeBlockTabsList>\n    <CodeBlockTabsTrigger value=\"Install\">\n      Install\n    </CodeBlockTabsTrigger>\n  </CodeBlockTabsList>\n\n  <CodeBlockTab value=\"Install\">\n    ```bash\n    npm install @seedcli/config\n    ```\n  </CodeBlockTab>\n</CodeBlockTabs>\n\nRequires Node.js >= 24.0.0.\n\nThe config module uses [c12](https://github.com/unjs/c12) (the config loader that powers Nuxt) to load configuration from multiple file formats with layered merging.\n\nLoading Config [#loading-config]\n\n```ts\nconst result = await seed.config.load<MyConfig>('myapp')\n```\n\nThis searches for config files in the following order:\n\n1. `myapp.config.ts`\n2. `myapp.config.js`\n3. `myapp.config.mjs`\n4. `myapp.config.json`\n5. `.myapprc`\n6. `.myapprc.json`\n7. `.myapprc.yaml`\n8. `.myapprc.toml`\n9. `package.json` → `myapp` field\n\nLoad Options [#load-options]\n\n| Option        | Type                | Description                                  |\n| ------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `name`        | `string`            | Config name to search for (required)         |\n| `defaults`    | `Partial<T>`        | Default configuration values                 |\n| `overrides`   | `Partial<T>`        | Override values (highest precedence)         |\n| `cwd`         | `string`            | Working directory (default: `process.cwd()`) |\n| `envName`     | `string`            | Environment name for env-specific overrides  |\n| `dotenv`      | `boolean`           | Load `.env` files                            |\n| `packageJson` | `boolean \\| string` | Read from `package.json` field               |\n| `rcFile`      | `boolean \\| string` | Read RC file                                 |\n| `globalRc`    | `boolean`           | Check global RC file                         |\n\nResult [#result]\n\n```ts\ninterface ResolvedConfig<T> {\n  config: T             // Merged config object\n  cwd: string           // Resolved working directory\n  configFile?: string   // Path to the config file found\n  layers: ConfigLayer[] // All config layers\n}\n\ninterface ConfigLayer {\n  config: Record<string, unknown>\n  source?: string       // Where this config came from\n  sourceOptions?: Record<string, unknown>\n}\n```\n\nDefault Values [#default-values]\n\n```ts\ninterface AppConfig {\n  outputDir: string\n  verbose: boolean\n  plugins: string[]\n}\n\nconst { config } = await seed.config.load<AppConfig>('myapp', {\n  defaults: {\n    outputDir: 'dist',\n    verbose: false,\n    plugins: [],\n  },\n})\n// config.outputDir is guaranteed to be a string\n```\n\nLoading a Specific File [#loading-a-specific-file]\n\n```ts\nconst config = await seed.config.loadFile<{ port: number }>('config/server.json')\n```\n\nGetting Nested Values [#getting-nested-values]\n\nUse dot-notation or bracket-notation to access nested config values:\n\n```ts\n// Dot notation\nconst port = seed.config.get(config, 'server.port')\n\n// Bracket notation\nconst host = seed.config.get({ 'server.host': 'localhost' }, '[server.host]', 'localhost')\n```\n\nThe `get` function takes an object and a path string, with an optional default value.\n\nBuilder Integration [#builder-integration]\n\nWhen using the Builder API, config is loaded automatically:\n\n```ts\nconst runtime = build('my-cli')\n  .config({\n    name: 'myapp',\n    defaults: {\n      outputDir: 'dist',\n      verbose: false,\n    },\n  })\n  .create()\n```\n\nThe user creates a config file:\n\n```ts title=\"myapp.config.ts\"\nexport default {\n  outputDir: 'build',\n  verbose: true,\n}\n```\n\nEnd-user config files loaded by `@seedcli/config` should export a plain object. `defineConfig()` from `@seedcli/core` is only for framework `seed.config.ts` files.\n\nEnvironment-Specific Config [#environment-specific-config]\n\n```ts\nconst { config } = await seed.config.load('myapp', {\n  envName: 'production',\n})\n```\n\nThis additionally searches for `myapp.config.production.ts` and merges it over the base config.\n\nConfig Layers [#config-layers]\n\nThe config system merges multiple layers in order of precedence:\n\n```\n1. defaults (lowest)\n2. config file\n3. environment-specific config\n4. package.json field\n5. overrides (highest)\n```\n\n```ts\nconst result = await seed.config.load('myapp', {\n  defaults: { port: 3000 },\n})\n\n// Inspect all layers\nfor (const layer of result.layers) {\n  console.log(`${layer.source}: ${JSON.stringify(layer.config)}`)\n}\n```\n";
