let _markdown$9 = "\n\n<CodeBlockTabs defaultValue=\"Install\">\n  <CodeBlockTabsList>\n    <CodeBlockTabsTrigger value=\"Install\">\n      Install\n    </CodeBlockTabsTrigger>\n\n    <CodeBlockTabsTrigger value=\"Import\">\n      Import\n    </CodeBlockTabsTrigger>\n  </CodeBlockTabsList>\n\n  <CodeBlockTab value=\"Install\">\n    ```bash\n    npm install @seedcli/patching\n    ```\n  </CodeBlockTab>\n\n  <CodeBlockTab value=\"Import\">\n    ```ts\n    import { append, exists, patch, patchJson, prepend } from '@seedcli/patching'\n    ```\n  </CodeBlockTab>\n</CodeBlockTabs>\n\nInside a Seed command, these same helpers are available on `seed.patching.*`.\n\nThe patching module lets you modify existing files by inserting, replacing, or deleting content at specific locations — ideal for code generation that needs to integrate with existing code.\n\nPatch a File [#patch-a-file]\n\n```ts\nconst result = await seed.patching.patch('src/app.ts', {\n  insert: \"import { logger } from './logger'\\n\",\n  before: \"import { router }\",\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.changed)  // true\n```\n\nPatch Options [#patch-options]\n\n| Option    | Type               | Description                                                   |\n| --------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `insert`  | `string`           | Content to insert (used with `before`, `after`, or `replace`) |\n| `before`  | `string \\| RegExp` | Insert before this pattern                                    |\n| `after`   | `string \\| RegExp` | Insert after this pattern                                     |\n| `replace` | `string \\| RegExp` | Pattern to replace (use with `insert` to provide replacement) |\n| `delete`  | `string \\| RegExp` | Pattern to delete                                             |\n\nPatch Result [#patch-result]\n\n| Property  | Type      | Description                   |\n| --------- | --------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `changed` | `boolean` | Whether the file was modified |\n| `content` | `string`  | The new file content          |\n\nExamples [#examples]\n\n**Insert before a pattern:**\n\n```ts\nawait seed.patching.patch('src/routes.ts', {\n  insert: \"  app.use('/api/users', usersRouter)\\n\",\n  before: '// END ROUTES',\n})\n```\n\n**Insert after a pattern:**\n\n```ts\nawait seed.patching.patch('src/index.ts', {\n  insert: \"import { analytics } from './analytics'\\n\",\n  after: \"import { app } from './app'\\n\",\n})\n```\n\n**Replace content:**\n\n```ts\nawait seed.patching.patch('config.json', {\n  replace: /\"version\": \"\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+\"/,\n  insert: '\"version\": \"2.0.0\"',\n})\n```\n\n**Delete content:**\n\n```ts\nawait seed.patching.patch('src/app.ts', {\n  delete: /import { oldModule } from '\\.\\/old-module'\\n/,\n})\n```\n\nAppend & Prepend [#append--prepend]\n\n```ts\n// Add content to the end of a file\nawait seed.patching.append('src/styles.css', '\\n.new-class { color: red; }\\n')\n\n// Add content to the beginning of a file\nawait seed.patching.prepend('src/app.ts', '// Generated file — do not edit\\n')\n```\n\nCheck for Pattern [#check-for-pattern]\n\nTest if a file contains a pattern:\n\n```ts\nconst hasImport = await seed.patching.exists(\n  'src/app.ts',\n  \"import { logger } from './logger'\"\n)\n\nconst hasRoute = await seed.patching.exists(\n  'src/routes.ts',\n  /app\\.use\\(['\"]\\/api\\/users['\"]/\n)\n\nif (!hasRoute) {\n  await seed.patching.patch('src/routes.ts', {\n    insert: \"  app.use('/api/users', usersRouter)\\n\",\n    before: '// END ROUTES',\n  })\n}\n```\n\nPatch JSON [#patch-json]\n\nModify JSON files with a mutation function:\n\n```ts\nawait seed.patching.patchJson<{ scripts?: Record<string, string> }>('package.json', (data) => {\n  data.scripts ??= {}\n  data.scripts.lint = 'biome check'\n  data.scripts.format = 'biome format --write'\n  return data\n})\n\n// Typed\ninterface PkgJson {\n  name: string\n  dependencies: Record<string, string>\n}\n\nawait seed.patching.patchJson<PkgJson>('package.json', (data) => {\n  data.dependencies['new-dep'] = '^1.0.0'\n  return data\n})\n```\n\nCommon Patterns [#common-patterns]\n\nAdding a route to an Express/Hono app [#adding-a-route-to-an-expresshono-app]\n\n```ts\nconst routeExists = await seed.patching.exists(\n  'src/routes.ts',\n  `app.use('/api/${name}'`\n)\n\nif (!routeExists) {\n  // Add import\n  await seed.patching.patch('src/routes.ts', {\n    insert: `import { ${name}Router } from './routes/${name}'\\n`,\n    after: /import .* from '\\.\\/routes\\/.*'\\n/,\n  })\n\n  // Add route\n  await seed.patching.patch('src/routes.ts', {\n    insert: `  app.use('/api/${name}', ${name}Router)\\n`,\n    before: '// END ROUTES',\n  })\n}\n```\n\nAdding an export to a barrel file [#adding-an-export-to-a-barrel-file]\n\n```ts\nawait seed.patching.append(\n  'src/index.ts',\n  `export { ${name} } from './${name}'\\n`\n)\n```\n";
